{
  "head": { "text": "Historical full-AHB SPLIT / RETRY mechanics (not part of AHB-Lite)" },
  "config": { "hscale": 2 },
  "signal": [
    [
      "Full-AHB arbiter signals",
      { "name": "HBUSREQ0", "wave": "0.1.........." },
      { "name": "HBUSREQ1", "wave": "0....1......." },
      { "name": "HGRANT0", "wave": "0.10....10..." },
      { "name": "HGRANT1", "wave": "0....10......" },
      { "name": "HSPLIT0", "wave": "0......10...." }
    ],
    {},
    [
      "Deferred and retried transfer",
      { "name": "HCLK", "wave": "P............" },
      { "name": "address master", "wave": "x.=xx=xx2x...", "data": ["M0", "M1", "M0 retry"] },
      { "name": "HTRANS", "wave": "x.=xx=xx2x...", "data": ["NONSEQ M0", "NONSEQ M1", "NONSEQ M0"] },
      { "name": "HADDR[31:0]", "wave": "x.=xx=xx2x...", "data": ["0x7000", "0x7100", "0x7000"] },
      { "name": "HRESP[1:0]", "wave": "x..=.x.......", "data": ["SPLIT"] },
      { "name": "HREADY", "wave": "1..01........" }
    ]
  ],
  "foot": {
    "text": "Historical full AHB only: SPLIT is a two-cycle response (HREADY low then high) that parks M0 until HSPLIT0 re-enables it. RETRY used the same response timing but did not use HSPLIT. Neither SPLIT nor RETRY exists in AHB-Lite."
  }
}
